// Coined quantum walk — one step on a 4-node cycle (positions 0-3,
// wrapping). The other major search paradigm alongside Grover's.
//
// `coin` decides direction, `lo`/`hi` hold the 2-bit position. Flip the
// coin into superposition, then shift +1 on coin=1 and -1 on coin=0 —
// both shifts run every time, each acting as identity on the branch it
// doesn't match, which is what keeps both directions in superposition.

qubit coin, lo, hi

H coin

// Controlled-increment on coin=1: standard 2-bit incrementer, CCX for
// the carry, CNOT for the low bit.
CCX coin lo hi
CNOT coin lo

// Controlled-decrement on coin=0: same incrementer, X-sandwiched so it
// triggers on coin=0 instead.
X coin
CNOT coin lo
CCX coin lo hi
X coin

MEASURE

// quell run quantum_walk.quell
// From position 0: lands entirely on positions 1 and 3 (~50/50), 0 and 2
// get nothing. A classical random walk would still leave mass at 0.
